Founding Story

eHarmony was founded on August 22, 2000, by
Dr. Neil Clark Warren, a 65-year-old clinical
psychologist. Dr. Warren spent the majority of his
career counseling married couples and speaking
out on how men and women develop healthy
marriage relationships. He came to the conclusion
that the single biggest factor that determines a
marriage’s success is picking the right partner. He
also felt he had a keen sense of the dimensions of
compatibility that led to a good match. Determined
to do something about it, Dr. Warren launched
eHarmony to leverage the power of the Internet to

