appearance resulted in 100,000 new subscribers
to eHarmony’s Web site, and the company was off
and running.

How It Works

eHarmony users fill out a 436-question
questionnaire that produces a personality
profile. Some of the questions, like “I work much
better if people follow my lead,” are answered
ona 1 to 5 scale; and others, like “Other than
your parents, who has been the most influential
person in your life, and why?” are fill in the blank.
The site then gives you a set of potential
matches—usually five at a time. Unlike other
matchmaking sites you can’t browse through
profiles and pick who you'd like to contact. You
only get access to the potential matches that
eHarmony provides you. It costs $59 a month

